<article class="env-definition" id="02SO">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02SO">Definition <span data-tag="02SO">42.25.1</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. We define, for every integer $k$, an operation </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c_1(\mathcal{L}) \cap - : Z_{k + 1}(X) \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> called <em>intersection with the first Chern class of $\mathcal{L}$</em>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Given an integral closed subscheme $i : W \to X$ with $\dim _\delta (W) = k + 1$ we define 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  c_1(\mathcal{L}) \cap [W] = i_*(c_1({i^*\mathcal{L}}) \cap [W])  \]
</div>
<p>
 where the right hand side is defined in Definition <a href="/tag/02SJ" data-tag="02SJ">42.24.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For a general $(k + 1)$-cycle $\alpha = \sum n_ i [W_ i]$ we set 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  c_1(\mathcal{L}) \cap \alpha = \sum n_ i c_1(\mathcal{L}) \cap [W_ i]  \]
</div>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>